<Bindings>
    <!--
        The only reason this file exists: a key the player can press mid-pull. A slash
        command is not usable when both hands are busy, which is precisely when something
        worth photographing tends to be happening.

        The header and the binding's name are labelled by BINDING_HEADER_CHRONIE and
        BINDING_NAME_CHRONIE_CAPTURE, declared in Main.lua. Without those globals the Key
        Bindings panel shows these raw tokens instead.

        ChronieCapture is set once the addon has wired itself together, so a key pressed
        before then does nothing rather than firing into a half-built addon.
    -->
    <Binding name="CHRONIE_CAPTURE" header="CHRONIE">
        if ChronieCapture then ChronieCapture() end
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
